 "note": "Private IPA 669 on the delivered and verified 666: the next common delivery, after every handoff of this round (MeloNX Core 667 handed over 6 November; no skins handoff pending). RPCS3 Core 668 (Core 665 with the thread orchestrator v1 removed by the maintainer: every Core file back to Core 664, which keeps the PPU grace after starvation; the host test page row removed; MoltenVK dependency of run 42051417882, same library bytes) replaces Core 665; MeloNX Core 667 (JIT arena per process, render worker buffer-array crash, Hogwarts precise math, shader save counters) replaces Core 663; the RPCS3 profile library returns Assassin's Creed IV: Black Flag to the PPU LLVM decoder over the official entry. Known cost (MeloNX session): with a process budget of 6 GiB or more, every first MeloNX launch maps a 1 GiB JIT arena whose pages the helper writes, about 512 MiB more footprint than before for titles other than Hogwarts. No iPhone measurement; no FPS claim.",
